// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Ghost-link acceptance fixture, a two-player co-op set-piece. All coordinates
// below are Quake map units.
// Two corresponding copies of one room: copy A centred at 0 0 and copy B at
// 4096 0, so the copies sit about 104 metres apart, farther than the 60 metre
// dev mod attenuation maxDistance. A real voice in one copy never reaches the
// other. Each room has an east doorway, y -64 to 64, into a back room, x 208
// to 432, and a low green cover wall west of the doorway. Only copy A doorway
// holds the yellow barrier mover; copy B doorway stays open. Openings a
// monster must path through are 128 units wide: the baked navmesh routes
// nothing through a 64 unit gap.
// Back room B holds the red button switch on its north wall and the green
// return pedestal, a mover sunk below its floor by the east wall. Back room A
// opens on the final-wave closet in its east wall, x 448 to 544, y -64 to 64,
// in line with the doorway so its monsters see into room A once its door
// sinks.
// Two ghost links tagged vault_echo, both styled echo, each covering a room and
// its back room. echo_a ghosts copy A into copy B, armed on spawn, listing the
// barrier tag. echo_b ghosts copy B into copy A, disarmed until the echo plate
// reveal. Each link volume reaches below the floor so the sinking barrier
// stays a member until it is out of sight.
// Barrier puzzle: press the red button in back room B. The barrier in copy A
// drops into the floor, and its ghost drops in copy B doorway.
// Monster closets: each copy hides monsters in two closets sealed by purple
// doors. The north closet opens x 32 to 160 and the south closet x -64 to 64
// in copy A, plus 4096 in copy B. Each is 96 units deep and full room height,
// so a monster eye clears its ceiling. Copy A north closet, door tag
// echo_closet_a1, holds two knights, reference_enemy, tagged echo_monster_a1;
// copy A south closet, door tag echo_closet_a2, holds one knight tagged
// echo_monster_a2. Copy B closets, door tag echo_closet_b, hold one limitator
// each, tagged echo_monster_b. Their sealed aggro gate, enabled_on_spawn 0,
// ignores even damage until a script wakes them. These closets sit outside
// the swap teleporter and ghost link volumes, and both copies build them
// alike, so the copies still line up.
// North closet: it opens fifteen seconds after level load, or as soon as a
// player touches the barrier_approach volume in front of copy A barrier,
// x 128 to 192, y -64 to 64, whichever comes first.
// Split: the first press of the purple use pad in either copy sends whoever
// stands on it alone into the other copy, through the seamless split teleporter
// laid over each pad. The crossing sinks copy A south closet door and wakes
// its knight at once, and three seconds later sinks both copy B closet doors
// and wakes the limitators.
// Flip: once the split lands, every press of a purple pad arms both seamless
// swap teleporters, so everyone standing in either room lands in the other
// copy. The first teleport through either swap teleporter disarms both, and
// the next press arms them again.
// Return: once copy B monsters are cleared the return pedestal rises and its
// purple use pad arms. A press arms the classic teleporter over the pad, which
// sends whoever stands there alone to return_a in room A, then disarms. The
// arrival turns the purple swap pads off for good and starts the final wave:
// the barrier drops if it still stands, and three seconds later the final
// closet door sinks and two knights and two limitators wake. A second arrival
// starts nothing again. No placed monster opts into ghosting.
// The blue touch plate in either copy runs echo.reveal and echo.swell.
// Player spawn 1 is in copy A and spawn 2, coop_only, in copy B. Body centres
// are 40 units up.
// An animated-bake lamp in each back room near the doorway, tagged
// alcove_lamp, shines out through the doorway. The ghost capture forces it to
// two colours: the scene around the ghost relights, the unlit ghost does not
// change.
// Cheap bake: one quarter metre per lightmap texel. No compiled output is
// committed.
// NOTE: keep map comments free of braces and quotes, and never leave a blank
// line inside an entity block.
{
"classname" "worldspawn"
"wad" ""
"data_script" "../scripts/ghost-links.luau"
"_tb_mod" "dev"
"_tb_def" "external:../../../sdk/TrenchBroom/postretro.fgd"
"_lightmap_density" "0.25"
